## 🧠 Strategic Enhancements Included

   1. Framework-Safe Event Dispatching: Modern frontend applications (React, Angular, Vue) maintain an internal virtual DOM state. Modifying an input element's raw .value directly using standard scripts will often cause form submissions to skip fields because the underlying JavaScript framework doesn't recognize the changes. Dispatching manual global input and change bubbling events ensures framework state compliance.
   2. Post-Submission Graph Capture: When a form is successfully fired, the browser captures the destination layout state footprint (postSubmitFingerprint). If the action routes to a completely new zone (e.g., an invoice view or error breakdown screen), that system node is parsed and added straight into the BFS pathing structure.
   3. State Engine Resets: After parsing a single form mutation sequence, the crawler enforces a complete application reset loop back to the base target route node string (page.goto(url)). This ensures subsequent test variations execute within an identical clean state structure environment.

